# Runtime artifacts. Never tracked.
#
# Worker logs contain full task text and model output, and .state files are
# per-host resume pointers -- neither is source, and both would leak operator
# content into history. Environment files are excluded so a credential cannot
# reach a commit even by accident (Phase 0 requirement: credentials are loaded
# from the environment and must not be committable).

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

*.log
*.state

# Written before a model runs and cleared after its result is reported, so a
# leftover one means the process died mid-task. Per-host runtime state, never
# source -- and committing one would tell every other checkout that a task it
# has never heard of was interrupted.
*.inflight

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.secret
secrets.json
